    "explanation": "Fairness MAD is a nonlinear function of aggregate exposure divided by aggregate opportunity, followed by a mean absolute deviation across cells. The expectation of this nonlinear statistic under cluster resampling need not equal its value at the observed aggregate totals. The discrepancy is therefore a bootstrap bias/curvature diagnostic, not by itself evidence of a coding error. It must be interpreted alongside exact archive reproduction and the jackknife."
